---
// The Supabase half of the boundary cdn-script.astro pins for Clerk, and the one PK-19
// made reachable: `@supabase/ssr` is a runtime dependency now, so an import specifier for
// it is a thing somebody can plausibly type — and typed as a URL, in an inline module
// script, it produces ZERO edges for the module graph to walk. Invariants A, B, C and D
// are all blind to this page, correctly, because there is no import here for a bundler to
// resolve.
//
// Caught only by the scan of the emitted HTML. Until PK-19 that scan named Clerk hosts
// and nothing else, so this exact page would have shipped the whole GoTrue stack to every
// visitor with the suite green.
---

<script is:inline type="module">
  import { createBrowserClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@supabase/ssr@0.12.4';
  window.__packsheetLeak = createBrowserClient;
</script>
<p>supabase cdn script</p>
